mend that you read if you have not done so already.\n     </p>\n     <p>\n      <b>\n       I have added Amazon affiliate program links to all these books.\n      </b>\n     </p>\n     <h4>\n      Highly Recommend\n     </h4>\n     <ul>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Don't Make Me Think: A Common Sense Approach to Web Usability\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Steve Krug\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Web Form Design: Filling in the Blanks\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Luke Wroblewski\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Getting Real: The smarter, faster, easier way to build a successful web Application\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Jason Fried\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Soak Wash Rinse Spin\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Tolleson Design\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n     </ul>\n     <h4>\n      Recommended\n     </h4>\n     <ul>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Bulletproof Web Design: Improving flexibility and protecting against worst-case scenarios with XHTML and CSS (2nd Edition)\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Dan Cederholm\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Eric Meyer on CSS: Mastering the Language of Web Design\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Eric Meyer\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Designing Web Usability\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Jakob Nielsen\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         The Art &amp; Science of Web Design\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Jeffrey Veen\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n     </ul>\n     <h5>\n      Non-Technology Books\n     </h5>\n     <ul>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         What Should I Do with My Life?: The True Story of People Who Answered the Ultimate Question\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Bo Bronson\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Oz Clarke's New Essential Wine Book: An Indispensable Guide to Wines of the World\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Oz Clarke\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n     </ul>\n     <h4>\n      Currently Reading\n     </h4>\n     <p>\n      The list of books below is books I am currently in the middle of or have not yet finished books.\n     </p>\n     <ul>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         DOM Scripting: Web Design with JavaScript and the Document Object Model\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Jeremy Keith\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         The Design of Everyday Things\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Donald A. Norman\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Train of Thoughts: Designing the Effective Web Experience (Voices)\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by: John C. Lenker, Jr.\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Speed Up Your Site: Web Site Optimization\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Andrew B. King\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n     </ul>\n     <h4>\n      Still to Read\n     </h4>\n     <p>\n      The following is a list of books I have purchased and have not yet had the time to read.\n     </p>\n     <ul>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Just Ask: Integrating Accessibility Throughout Design\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Shawn Lawton Henry\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Web Accessibility: Web Standards and Regulatory Compliance\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by: multiple authors\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Designing with Web Standards (3rd Edition)\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Jeffrey Zeldman\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <p>\n        <a>\n         Universal Design for Web Applications: Web Applications That Reach Everyone\n        </a>\n       </p>\n       <p>\n        by:\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Wendy Chisholm\n        </a>\n        and\n        <a class=\"author\">\n         Matt May\n        </a>\n       </p>\n      </li>\n     </ul>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n   <div id=\"footer\">\n    <div id=\"navbar_b\">\n     <ul id=\"nav_b\" role=\"navigation\">\n      <li>\n       <a>\n        About\n       </a>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <a>\n        Accessibility\n       </a>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <a>\n        Blog\n       </a>\n      </li>\n      <li>\n       <a>\n        Books\n       </a>\n      </li>\n     </ul>\n     <p role=\"contentinfo\">\n      &copy; 2007 - 2019\n      <a>\n       jfciii.com\n      </a>\n     </p>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n </body>\n</html>\n",
